## Customize flags given to the VM: https://www.erlang.org/doc/man/erl.html
## -mode/-name/-sname/-setcookie are configured via env vars, do not set them here

## Erlang "ports" (NOT port numbers: the VM's handles to the outside — every
## network connection, the Unix socket's included; files aren't ports since
## OTP 21) the VM may hold at once — one per connected person. Linux's
## default is 65536 (Windows: 8192). 1048576 = the most Linux lets one program
## open (fs.nr_open) and systemd's ceiling; it reserves ~15 MB at start-up
## (measured in WSL: 31 → 46 MB; 16M would be 286 MB). Pairs with
## LimitNOFILE=1048576 in deploy/hoodride.service — change them together.
## Memory and CPU run out long before this.
+Q 1048576

## The node's own port (for `bin/hoodride rpc` / `remote`) on 127.0.0.1 only —
## by default it listens on every address. epmd: ERL_EPMD_ADDRESS in env.sh.eex.
-kernel inet_dist_use_interface {127,0,0,1}

## Tweak GC to run more often
##-env ERL_FULLSWEEP_AFTER 10
